INV-lalad added `instantiates` to TAINT_CALL_EDGE_TYPES so the taint walk could
traverse construction edges. That is recall work landing into measurement
0001's pre-registered `<50%` band, whose stated rule is that recall work should
stop until precision is understood. I shipped it and had not measured the
precision half. This is that measurement.

DESIGN: a delta census, not a re-run. 0001's census population was 60 flows on
2026-08-11; the same five repos produce 298 at this fix's parent commit nine
days later, so a re-run would have pooled 238 flows of unrelated drift into this
change's account. Baseline 148fae52b3 in an ephemeral clone, subject
d8d415dd0d, the same instrument from the working tree in both arms, and an
isolated XDG_CACHE_HOME per arm so neither could read the other's cached
behaviour map. The control was verified before any number was read: under the
baseline path the interpreter resolves taint.py to the clone and reports
{calls, dispatches_to, module_attr_ref}; unshadowed it adds instantiates.

RESULT: 35 added, 0 removed, all adjudicated, none unadjudicable. 1 TP, 34 FP —
2.9% marginal precision against ≈41%.

The true positive is this item's own thesis confirmed on a second sink:
mitmproxy binds os.path.expanduser to `p`, passes it to write_magisk_module,
and magisk.py:100 is `ZipFile(path, "w")`. Invisible before the fix for exactly
the subprocess.Popen reason.

The false positives are one dominant mechanism: 24 of 34 land on 10 call sites
that are ALL constructors taking no arguments, a keyword literal, a generated
temp path, or the temp-file object — checked exhaustively across every
constructor call site in all five pretix files, not only the reported ones. A
zero-argument call cannot carry taint by argument and its receiver is a module,
so that is a proof rather than a heuristic. Filed as INV-fubag (P1), with an
explicit requirement that any fix preserve the mitmproxy true positive, since
killing both would read as success on FP count alone.

Not a new defect. content-not-argument and co-location-function were already 29
of 0001's 57 false positives; this change fed a large new class of sinks into an
existing, documented weakness. The fix stays: backing out `instantiates` would
re-hide subprocess.Popen(tainted).

Honest limit, recorded in the document: single adjudication pass by the author
of the change measured, where 0001 used blind second passes. The bias runs
against the reported result, and 24 of the 34 verdicts are mechanical.

